title: Estimate form for concrete (free PDF) | Jobchit
description: A free, printable concrete estimate form. Area and thickness, yards, mix and PSI, rebar or mesh, base and excavation, finish, line items and total, with a line for the customer to sign. No account needed.
heading: Estimate for concrete
sub: Size, thickness, mix, base and finish on one page, with line items, a total and a line for the customer to sign when they say yes.
tips:
  - Give the area as length, width and thickness, and say what is being poured: slab, driveway, walk, patio or footing.
  - Write the yardage and the mix, such as PSI and any air entrainment or fiber, so the customer can see what the price covers.
  - Say what is under and inside the pour: base or sub-base, forms, rebar or mesh, and who handles digging and haul-off.
  - Record the finish, any color or stamp pattern, control joints and sealer, and whether demolition of old concrete is included.
  - Say who pulls any permit and whether weather or site access can change the price. Put a date the price is good until, and when the customer agrees, have them sign and date it.
